{"id": "EUVD-2026-102352", "enisaUuid": "92b3f69f-27ed-3a3e-9dde-26b11e1029dc", "description": "AdPlug through 2.4 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in CdmoLoader::load() in src/dmo.cpp that allows attackers to read past a heap allocation by supplying a truncated TwinTeam DMO file. Attackers can supply a 12- or 13-byte file passing dmo_unpacker::decrypt(), opened via CAdPlug::factory, to read bytes beyond packed_module and potentially crash the application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:56:53", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/adplug-ksm-note-loop-databuf-oob-write", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug/blob/e491e382479ed2246f124c96c70d94561dce59b9/src/dmo.cpp#L56-L78", "https://github.com/adplug/adplug", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/adplug-through-2.4-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-cdmoloader-load"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110877", "GHSA-w9c2-q7vc-jhg6"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3417910c-7bd4-348d-865c-e6c3f8af1298", "product": {"name": "adplug", "vendor": {"name": "adplug"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c3bc2eaf-f73c-34ae-ad52-fd7ef73594a0", "vendor": {"name": "adplug"}}], "isExploited": false}